hostapd.uc: restart every radio of an MLD when one of them restarts

Restarting one radio breaks every AP MLD it shares with the other radios,
and nothing brings them back. Measured on BPI-R4/MT7996 with udebug,
2026-09-18, every time: radio0 alone -> ap-mld-2 (no BSS on radio0) lost
both links; radio1 or radio2 alone -> ap-mld-1 and ap-mld-2 left with one
link each. A full `wifi` always recovers.

Three layers: mac80211 stops every non-transmitting MBSSID member with all
its MLD links when the transmitting BSS stops; hostapd frees the driver
state the other links of an MLD still point at when the link that created
the netdev goes; and the restart path only brings back the restarted radio.

When a radio that was running with MLD links stops or changes, the other
running radios of those MLDs are restarted too after 3 s - all taken down
first, then brought up. During a full `wifi` they are torn down by netifd
within that time and skipped. With this, single-radio restarts keep 3/3 and
2/2 links on all three radios.

--- a/hostapd.uc	2026-09-18 18:37:55.765435795 +0200
+++ b/hostapd.uc	2026-09-18 18:37:55.833334877 +0200
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 let libubus = require("ubus");
 import { open, readfile, access } from "fs";
+import * as uloop from "uloop";
 import { wdev_remove, is_equal, vlist_new, phy_is_fullmac, phy_open, wdev_set_radio_mask, wdev_set_up } from "common";
 
 let ubus = libubus.connect(null, 60);
@@ -1177,6 +1178,102 @@
